  "summary": "Designed for festive gatherings, this showstopping Lebanese celebration stew centers on tender <b>lamb shoulder shanks</b> braised in a saffron pomegranate broth. Marinated with seven spices, sumac, and garlic, the lamb is seared until deeply browned before simmering slowly with sweet shallots and dried figs. Pomegranate molasses and fresh pomegranate arils infuse the broth with rich ruby color and vibrant tart contrast. Tender chickpeas and roasted butternut squash chunks melt into the silky sauce, absorbing warm cinnamon and clove aromatics. Finished with toasted pine nuts, slivered almonds, and fresh mint, this dish offers magnificent texture and fragrance. Served over fragrant golden saffron rice, it forms the centerpiece of traditional feast tables. Rich, spicy, and fruit-scented, this special-occasion stew honors classic Levantine culinary heritage in every savory bite.",
